Subject: [PATCH] usb: hub: skip OTG root-hub debounce during B-host activation
Upstream-Status: Pending

hub_is_b_host_otg_port() had fallen back to "|| true" because
bus->is_b_host does not read true during activation on this platform,
which matched every hub port rather than only the root hub's OTG port.
That was harmless while this function had a single caller during B-host
activation, but 0040-usb-hub-skip-connect-debounce-on-the-OTG-root-port.
patch added a second caller on the accessory role-switch path, and the
same over-broad match there skips the connect debounce on ordinary
downstream hubs and devices too. Fixed by keying purely on port identity
(root hub + the HCD's registered OTG port) instead of the unreliable
is_b_host bit.

---
 drivers/usb/core/hub.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
index 256fe8c86..c28990d28 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
@@ -1080,6 +1080,25 @@ enum hub_activation_type {
 static void hub_init_func2(struct work_struct *ws);
 static void hub_init_func3(struct work_struct *ws);

+/*
+ * During HNP the OTG port on the root hub is a protocol-controlled soft
+ * connection. Skip the normal 100-ms connect debounce for that port while
+ * activating the hub as a B-host.
+ *
+ * bus->is_b_host does not reliably reflect B-host activation on this
+ * platform (it reads back as A-host instead), so this keys purely on port
+ * identity: the root hub's designated OTG port. Both this function's
+ * callers - this one and the accessory role-switch one in
+ * 0040-usb-hub-skip-connect-debounce-on-the-OTG-root-port.patch - depend
+ * on that scope; an earlier "|| true" fallback here matched every hub
+ * port instead, skipping the connect debounce on ordinary downstream
+ * hubs and devices too.
+ */
+static bool hub_is_b_host_otg_port(struct usb_device *hdev, int port1)
+{
+	return !hdev->parent && hdev->bus->otg_port == port1;
+}
+
 static void hub_activate(struct usb_hub *hub, enum hub_activation_type type)
 {
 	struct usb_device *hdev = hub->hdev;
@@ -1234,7 +1253,8 @@ static void hub_activate(struct usb_hub *hub, enum hub_activation_type type)

 		/* Clear status-change flags; we'll debounce later */
 		if (portchange & USB_PORT_STAT_C_CONNECTION) {
-			need_debounce_delay = true;
+			if (!hub_is_b_host_otg_port(hdev, port1))
+				need_debounce_delay = true;
 			usb_clear_port_feature(hub->hdev, port1,
 					USB_PORT_FEAT_C_CONNECTION);
 		}
-- 
